Without explanation I would interpret the data in the following way
(CMIIW). The "Damage" row shows the damage of MB's special attacks.
The percentages reflect the probabilities that those special attacks
occur. And the rightmost column considers damage and percentage, and
shows the average damage done, taking all effects into account.

What I don't understand is the conclusion that MB is best at +2.
WRT its specific attacks I agree, and that's the reason why I also
try to leave it at +2. But some people consider damage as primary
factor; those people may consider +3 or +4 more damage points to be
better than some occasional scare, stun, or cancel attack.

As far as I've observed the discussions about Magicbane in the past,
it's not as clear to claim that it's best at +2; I suppose it lies
in the eye of the beholder.

Personally I think that such +3 more damage points is not worth the
enchantment. I've also ascended with Magicbane's little melee damage.

Wizards, who have Magicbane practically guaranteed, typically wouldn't
use a melee weapon anyway; they'd cast highly effective attack spells.
With other classes it depends; characters have multiple choices how
to deal with the game challenges (missiles, casts, melee, avoidance,
or specific solutions like rubber chickens, or any other option).

